<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maiden Tower</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Qız Qalası</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maiden Tower is a cylindrical stone tower about 29 metres high in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/icherisheher">Old City of Baku</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, standing near the old shoreline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>. Its date and purpose are disputed: parts may be pre-Islamic, while an inscription links building work to the 12th century. It is the city's best-known landmark and, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palace-of-the-shirvanshahs">Palace of the Shirvanshahs</a>, part of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> inscribed in 2000.</p></div>
